input.new_string:
/* The prompt-box glow ring (PromptHero) — a Gemini-style "chasing light"
   ring. CRITICAL: the ring's own box never rotates. Earlier versions
   animated `transform: rotate()` on the ring element itself, which — since
   the composer is a wide rectangle, not a square — swings the corners way
   outside the box's footprint at 30-60deg (a wide rect rotated about its
   center sweeps a much larger diamond-shaped envelope), then back into
   alignment near 0/90/180/270deg. That's what read as "a giant blob that
   then disappears": it never disappeared, it was cycling through a much
   bigger silhouette than the box. The fix is to keep the ring's shape
   perfectly static and instead animate the *angle fed into the conic
   gradient* via a registered custom property (@property is required for
   the browser to animate it smoothly rather than snapping) — the ring
   never moves, only the color chases around inside it. */
@property --glow-angle-a {
  syntax: "<angle>";
  inherits: false;
  initial-value: 0deg;
}
@property --glow-angle-b {
  syntax: "<angle>";
  inherits: false;
  initial-value: 180deg;
}
@keyframes glow-angle-spin-a {
  to {
    --glow-angle-a: 360deg;
  }
}
@keyframes glow-angle-spin-b {
  to {
    --glow-angle-b: -180deg;
  }
}
.glow-ring-a {
  animation: glow-angle-spin-a 6s linear infinite;
}
.glow-ring-b {
  animation: glow-angle-spin-b 9s linear infinite;
}

